course: dictionary
lesson: 7981
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word record can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action). Its meaning depends on the words around it, which is its context. Use the clues to choose the right meaning.
explain: Context shows the meaning. «Billie Eilish and her brother Finneas recorded much of her debut album on a computer.» Recorded is an action here: they saved the sound so it could be played again. A record can also be a written note of facts, as in «old records», or the best result ever, as in a world record.
explain: Say the word to hear the difference. As a noun, record is said REK-ord (a record of the rain). As a verb, it is said ri-KORD (to record the rain). Try putting your meaning into the sentence. If it still makes sense, you have found it.
fact: Record can be a noun (a thing) or a verb (an action).
fact: As a noun, «record» can mean a written note of facts, the best result ever, or a round flat disc that plays music.
fact: As a verb, «record» means to write down information, or to save sound or pictures so you can play them again.
fact: «A studbook records every animal of one kind in zoos.» Here records is a verb: it means writes down.
fact: Phrases such as «break a record», «keep a record» and «on record» use record in special ways.
exercise: «Apps let children record the animals and plants they see.» What does record mean here? | To sing very loudly | *To save photos or sound so you can look at them later | To break a world best | To play a round disc of music
exercise: «Some hold a bit of truth, and you can test them with a diary and old records.» What are old records here? | *Written notes of facts from the past | Round discs that play music | The best scores ever set | Videos of people playing games
exercise: «She broke the world record for the fastest swim.» What does record mean here? | *The best result ever | To write down information | To save sound for later | A round flat disc that plays music
test: «Historians reject this because there is no evidence in Chinese records, maps or archaeology.» What does records mean here? | The best results ever | A round disc for music | *Written notes of facts | To save sound | 
test: Mia says, «I will record the show on the television tonight.» What does record mean? | To sing the show's theme song | To break a record | To write down the facts about the show | *To save the show so you can watch it later
exam: Which meaning fits «He will record the results in a table» and why? | The best result ever, because the results are the highest | To save sound, because a table can hear | *To write down information, because the results go in a table | A round flat disc, because music plays from a table
